{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039219-why-i-hate-sorcerers-rules-or-why-they-don-t-fit-in-mage","id":1039219,"title":"Why I hate sorcerers rules, or why they don't fit in Mage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-27T19:46:26-08:00","id":1039219,"title":"Why I hate sorcerers rules, or why they don't fit in Mage","content":"So, one thing that has always bothered me: sorcerers.<br /> <br /> I mean, they are just another kind of weak supernaturals, not exactly guys that works &quot;consensual magik&quot;.<br /> <br /> According to Mage, when I turn my TV on, I'm making a Forces+Correspondence effect without knowing. All sleepers are &quot; sorcerers&quot; of sorts, or &quot;technosorcerers&quot; if you prefer.<br /> <br /> I don't have a list of pre defined &quot;powers&quot; that I need in order to use other &quot;effects&quot;. For example, I don't have:<br /> 1 dot - turn the TV on; change channels;<br /> 2 dots - Use a cellphone<br /> 3 dots - Use a computer<br /> 4 dots - Use the internet<br /> 5 dots - Play videogames<br /> <br /> That's just ridiculous and absurd.<br /> <br /> Besides, the powers of Sorcerers in books... Are completely unrelated to anything.<br /> <br /> They are simply thaumaturgical paths... But they should be related to PARADIGMS<br /> <br /> So, there should be <i>akashic</i> sorcerors; acolites that train meditation, breathing exercizes, that believe in the balance of the Chi, that practice martial arts.<br /> <br /> <i>Hermetic</i> sorcerors, that study exoteric geometry, elemental analogy, and so on<br /> <br /> <i>Virtual Adept</i> sorcery, which relies on computer programming and virtual reality<br /> <br /> <i>Technocratic &quot;Sorcery&quot;</i> based on strictly &quot;scientific&quot; views.<br /> <br /> Sorcery is a form of magik after all, but is static Magic. But the SOURCE of their power is the same: the <b><i><u>Avatar</u></i></b>. So, it's also paradigm based.<br /> <br /> The way I do it? Instead of giving &quot;disciplines&quot; to sorcerous, I give them <i>rotes</i>. That's right, I give sorcerers rotes from <i>Mages</i>. But, those rotes are static effects. For example: <u>Spiritual Ward against Wraiths (Spirit 2)</u>. The sorceror that learns that effect, can only use it <i>that way</i>. An effect &quot;Ward against wraiths except stygians&quot; (Spirit 4, Time 4, Entropy 2) is another effect and must be learned separatly.<br /> <br /> So, mechanics: I make all rotes as Knowledge Skills, therefore going from 1-5. Experience costs: level of the highest Sphere used for the effect multiplied for the current level on the effect. The first level always costs as much as the higher Sphere.<br /> <br /> For example: Fireballs (gotta love the classics). Forces 3, Prime 2. So, this &quot;skill&quot; will cost <br /> <br /> 1 dot - 3 XP<br /> 2 dots - 3 XP<br /> 3 dots - 6 XP<br /> 4 dots - 9 XP<br /> 5 dots - 12 XP<br /> <br /> An effect to turn the skin into steel - Life 4, Matter 2<br /> 1 dot - 4 XP<br /> 2 dot - 4 XP<br /> 3 dot - 8 XP<br /> 4 dot - 12 XP<br /> 5 dot - 16 XP<br /> <br /> So, all sorcerors would be paradigm dependent, and could actually do a few impressive things, but would be VERY restricted. And more: now, few people would REALLY be able to tell sorcerors and mages apart.<br /> <br /> For the dice roll: just roll the skill of the sorceror instead of Arete (so, sorcerors can't go beyond LVL 5, which I think is well within the concept, since Arete 6+ allows abandoning the foci - sorcerors can NEVER abandon their paradigms, because that would mean he would not be able to use the effect he learned)<br /> <br /> What do you guys think about that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T20:01:49-08:00","id":1039223,"title":"","content":"Did you read Sorcerers Revised? It is paradigm based.<br /> <br /> Their paths are the specific ways in which magic can be done, but the method is still paradigm. To heal, a Pagan Sorceror may do a ritual using a book of shadows as guidance, A Shaman type would instead chant a series of prayers to ask the spirits to leave the afflicted, while a Scientist may used a number of pills.<br /> <br /> Letting sorcerors do Rotes is not a good idea, allowing them anything close to awakened magic without a huge drawback is too gamebreaking. Why would anyone bother with awakening when all the cools stuff could be Paradox free?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T20:02:23-08:00","id":1039224,"title":"","content":"Sorcerers are not meant to be one trick ponies though, they were meant to be competent practitioners of linear magic that were capable of functioning in a crossover environment much more easily than Mages (the original Sorcerer book was a crossover book that had no more to do with MtA than it had to do with CtD, VtM, WtA, or WtO). Linear magic is also able to thumb its nose at the concepts of the Consensus and Paradox, though every form of linear magic is associated with some magical tradition. In addition, I like the fact that Sorcerers can own Mages by shutting down their effects every turn by using countermagic and, with each turn that Mages attempt vulgar magick that Sorcerers shut down, they risk a catastrophic botch (and probably waste valuable Quintessence).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T20:14:37-08:00","id":1039233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039219-why-i-hate-sorcerers-rules-or-why-they-don-t-fit-in-mage?p=1039223#post1039223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you read Sorcerers Revised? It is paradigm based.<br /> <br /> Their paths are the specific ways in which magic can be done, but the method is still paradigm. To heal, a Pagan Sorceror may do a ritual using a book of shadows as guidance, A Shaman type would instead chant a series of prayers to ask the spirits to leave the afflicted, while a Scientist may used a number of pills.<br /> <br /> Letting sorcerors do Rotes is not a good idea, allowing them anything close to awakened magic without a huge drawback is too gamebreaking. Why would anyone bother with awakening when all the cools stuff could be Paradox free?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because its expensive as hell. Most would just know one trick or two, maybe three. Unlike Mages that are limitless.<br /> <br /> The &quot;powers&quot; of the sorcerors are still just another kind of disciplines, with no connection with anything. Just losen set of powers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T20:23:57-08:00","id":1039235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039219-why-i-hate-sorcerers-rules-or-why-they-don-t-fit-in-mage?p=1039224#post1039224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorcerers are not meant to be one trick ponies though, they were meant to be competent practitioners of linear magic that were capable of functioning in a crossover environment much more easily than Mages (the original Sorcerer book was a crossover book that had no more to do with MtA than it had to do with CtD, VtM, WtA, or WtO). Linear magic is also able to thumb its nose at the concepts of the Consensus and Paradox, though every form of linear magic is associated with some magical tradition. In addition, I like the fact that Sorcerers can own Mages by shutting down their effects every turn by using countermagic and, with each turn that Mages attempt vulgar magick that Sorcerers shut down, they risk a catastrophic botch (and probably waste valuable Quintessence).</div> </div> </div> </div>Initiially, that idea came from &quot;Hunted Hunters&quot;, and they were supposed to play on crossovers with vampires. But that was before the game Mage existed. After that... Well... There were Mages already. No more need for those spellcasters.<br /> <br /> And after Mage, the concept of sorcerors became connected with mages.<br /> <br /> And no, sorcerors are NOT supposed to be a new breed of supernaturals... Much less &quot;supernatural normal humans&quot;. Their magic was to give an edgy, not turn them into a powerful new breed of nightfolk... And to make them with the felling that they are still normal humans, just with a few capabilities.<br /> <br /> Now, lets look at things: there are all those limited paths. You say &quot;it's paradigm related&quot;. Yeah. But they can't go on Astral Travel if that's not in a losen relation of disconnected powers, no matter how much he truly, truly, truly, believes that. That's what I don't like, I don't know if I were able to make myself clear here or not... 2:20 am here, starting to Sleepwalk...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T20:30:01-08:00","id":1039237,"title":"","content":"Well, the original Hunter's Hunter had Spells rather than Paths. Spells were single focus magical tricks that were purchased as Abilities and were linked to specific Mental Attributes. Paths ended up making the entire thing much more interesting (and Hedge Wizard's Handbook came out after Mage, so Sorcerers were obviously intended to be something other than Mages or Mage-light).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T02:49:10-08:00","id":1039326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039219-why-i-hate-sorcerers-rules-or-why-they-don-t-fit-in-mage?p=1039233#post1039233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because its expensive as hell. Most would just know one trick or two, maybe three. Unlike Mages that are limitless.<br /> <br /> The &amp;quot;powers&amp;quot; of the sorcerors are still just another kind of disciplines, with no connection with anything. Just losen set of powers</div> </div> </div> </div>At this point, I think you'll be better off just saying that you don't like the concept and don't support them in you games.<br /> <br /> The rest is giving off the vibe that you think nobody else should enjoy the concept and have fun with it either, which is a bad focus to have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T03:23:15-08:00","id":1039335,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12880\" data-vbnamecard=\"12880\">Karlgust</a><br /> \u200bI think the main problem you are having is that WoD is a kitchen sink setting. That means that the stories you tell with it will be set in a world that has a whole lot of stuff in it. There are more than a dozen varieties of vampires. There are more than twenty kinds of magic. There are ten million billion shapeshifter types. And that means that there are a lot of stories you can tell. It means that you can tell a story that revolves around any one of those unique types of vampires, or one that involves people using any of those kinds of magic. But there are also stories you cannot tell. You can't tell a story where, like in Lightbringer, there are strict rules of magic and everyone follows them. You can't tell a story where anyone is particularly surprised that they don't recognize some new shapeshifting monster, because there are so many of those things that hopping around that no one expects to be able to identify them all. In short, you can't tell a story where <i>uniqueness is unique</i>. Nor can you tell a story where the edges of things are well defined, because there are too many edges to define.<br /> <br /> &quot;Sorcery is static magic&quot; is a bullshit line meant to explain why vampires and werewolves don't explode in a cloud of paradox, because the world as Mage writers wrote it doesn't allow the existence of vampires and werewolves. It's a cludge meant to rectify the glaring error of world building. And it's a cludge that made WoD more of a kitchen sink than it was before. Personally, I like reductionist fantasy more than kitchen sink and would cut the sorcerers entirely given the chance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T04:12:01-08:00","id":1039356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039219-why-i-hate-sorcerers-rules-or-why-they-don-t-fit-in-mage?p=1039326#post1039326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At this point, I think you'll be better off just saying that you don't like the concept and don't support them in you games.<br /> <br /> The rest is giving off the vibe that you think nobody else should enjoy the concept and have fun with it either, which is a bad focus to have.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the concept actually, I just don't like it the way it is. And for anybody else, people can like or not, or can like as I putted or not, that's an individual choice","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T04:16:04-08:00","id":1039357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039219-why-i-hate-sorcerers-rules-or-why-they-don-t-fit-in-mage?p=1039335#post1039335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12880\" data-vbnamecard=\"12880\">Karlgust</a><br /> \u200bI think the main problem you are having is that WoD is a kitchen sink setting. That means that the stories you tell with it will be set in a world that has a whole lot of stuff in it. There are more than a dozen varieties of vampires. There are more than twenty kinds of magic. There are ten million billion shapeshifter types. And that means that there are a lot of stories you can tell. It means that you can tell a story that revolves around any one of those unique types of vampires, or one that involves people using any of those kinds of magic. But there are also stories you cannot tell. You can't tell a story where, like in Lightbringer, there are strict rules of magic and everyone follows them. You can't tell a story where anyone is particularly surprised that they don't recognize some new shapeshifting monster, because there are so many of those things that hopping around that no one expects to be able to identify them all. In short, you can't tell a story where <i>uniqueness is unique</i>. Nor can you tell a story where the edges of things are well defined, because there are too many edges to define.<br /> <br /> &quot;Sorcery is static magic&quot; is a bullshit line meant to explain why vampires and werewolves don't explode in a cloud of paradox, because the world as Mage writers wrote it doesn't allow the existence of vampires and werewolves. It's a cludge meant to rectify the glaring error of world building. And it's a cludge that made WoD more of a kitchen sink than it was before. Personally, I like reductionist fantasy more than kitchen sink and would cut the sorcerers entirely given the chance.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is, indeed, a problem. White Wolf wanted to keep printing books to keep the money flowing... And they turned the world into a freaking Circus.<br /> <br /> When Vampire started, you could choose your char from amongst 7 clans. <i>And that's it</i>. No Guide to the Sabbat, no players guide with independent clans, no nothing. Also, the disciplines would only reach level 5. &quot;Who knows what the elders can do?&quot; was a thing that added a lot in the games. What about those Tzimisce and Lasombra? Those were meant to be enemies. Their powers had no descriptions, just a few nuances, and that's why they are probably the two most monstruous powers - control over shadows and control over meat.<br /> <br /> In time, they would give all the 13 clans, and their powers. Not just that, they would give the powers of everything up to the 3th generation (which they would later regreat and roll back &quot;only&quot; to the 4th and let the vamp gods do whatever they like... Which were also a bad idea).<br /> <br /> So, the scenario of Vampire, which were about Camarilla vs Sabbat, became just the play stage of the antidiluvians... First of all, nothing can be done against them... Secondly, they are godlike... Third, they manipulate everyone... And forth, white Wolf told all their secrets, favorite places for vacations, etc. They were meant to be mysteries; they were meant to be a myth.<br /> <br /> On top of that... Yeah, lets keep pouring obscure minuscule bloodlines that dont really add anything to the scenario, but will satisfy that guy that wanna a new and obscure power that no one has ever heard about... Gargoyles, Children of Cacophony, Kyasid, Blood Brothers... WTF<br /> <br /> If you notice, from all the seven clans on Camarilla, there were only TWO unique powers: Metamorphosis and Thaumaturgy. And that's it.<br /> <br /> A few years latter they give the tips about the Sabbat. Please tell me how many bloodlines and exclusive powers...<br /> <br /> And all games suffered from this. In Werewolf, they gave the other Fera. Stupid and nonsensical things like sharkmen or dinomen. A gazillion of fomori (the boogeymen that can't scare a 5 years old child. &quot;Nah, another fomori freak, how boring).<br /> <br /> In Mage, luckly, that TERRIBLE and STUPID obssession of White Wolf to make new obscure and exclusive &quot;families&quot; of supernaturals utterly failed, thankfully. Not that they haven't tryed thou. It's just that &quot;Sister of Hyppolita&quot; don't really have any cool obscure power that nobody else have. That's why those crap crafts didn't stick, and people, at large, just ignore that COMPLETELY. In that aspect, Mage were luck that there are only 9 Spheres that can do anything; no run for secret albino Vietnamise cultists or Cambodjan cannibals or chinese shemales to have that unique power, that exclusive thaumaturgical line, oh, the only ones that have access to the abyss mysticism so I wanna split their skulls to steal it. <br /> <br /> No. All those freaks will have the same spheres as anybody else. And that has been a blessing for Mage, because it kept the game with it's original coherence. The game is Traditions vs Technocracy goddam!<br /> <br /> But of course White Wolf would never be happy to just let a good game keep it coherence... Oh please, don't be silly. If they didn't ruined it, it wouldn't be White Wolf. So, they had the brilliant idea of trashing both the Traditions and Technocracy. The Traditions now are just a bunch of punks, and the Techies some crazy lunatics. Not to mention all the pathetic metaplot about super powers to destroy the Ravanna. And now they've managed to utterly destroy the game's essence... Well done WW.<br /> <br /> Well, as consolation, Mage wasn't the only one they ruined. They did it with ALL games.<br /> <br /> Actually, wraith was luck for being cast on Oblivion, because that kept the game pure, unlike the others. Which is why is one of the best games at the moment (I just don't call it the best because I love Mage too much). No ghost small little families-clan-like that white Wolf loves so much, no &quot;book of secrets&quot; that have that exclusive ritual that only 2 persons in the world knows (but somehow, the players learn), no &quot;tome of lost supernatural-families-with-that-unique-power-that-has-no-relation-with-anything-whatsoever&quot;, no secret &quot;sub-families&quot;. Magnific game... Because White Wolf haven't had the time or effort to ruin it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","user":"Karlgust","date":". 01-28-2017, 08:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T04:22:25-08:00","id":1039359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039219-why-i-hate-sorcerers-rules-or-why-they-don-t-fit-in-mage#post1039219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, mechanics: I make all rotes as Knowledge Skills, therefore going from 1-5. Experience costs: level of the highest Sphere used for the effect multiplied for the current level on the effect. The first level always costs as much as the higher Sphere.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is both unnecessary complicated and too expensive. The price of becoming a master of Fireball is 33XP which usually means that you spent half of your campaign doing nothing but improving Fireball. Just have them cost as normal skills and regulate the number of dots that can be spent in chargen.<br /> <br /> The bigger question I have is what role do you see for sorcerers in the story? Since you are putting XP costs to things I assume you envision sorcerer PCs. What is the core sorcerer story? What do they do? Mages fight against the Technocracy. Vampires survive night to night upholding the Masquerade and squabble with each other. Werewolves run around commiting mass murder. What do sorcerers do? Are they lackeys to the Mages, a la ghoul game? Are they fighting against the Mages to gain avatars of their own?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039219-why-i-hate-sorcerers-rules-or-why-they-don-t-fit-in-mage?p=1039357#post1039357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is, indeed, a problem. White Wolf wanted to keep printing books to keep the money flowing... And the</div> </div> </div> </div>Your post kinda got eaten here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T05:15:54-08:00","id":1039375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039219-why-i-hate-sorcerers-rules-or-why-they-don-t-fit-in-mage?p=1039359#post1039359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is both unnecessary complicated and too expensive. The price of becoming a master of Fireball is 33XP which usually means that you spent half of your campaign doing nothing but improving Fireball. Just have them cost as normal skills and regulate the number of dots that can be spent in chargen.<br /> <br /> The bigger question I have is what role do you see for sorcerers in the story? Since you are putting XP costs to things I assume you envision sorcerer PCs. What is the core sorcerer story? What do they do? Mages fight against the Technocracy. Vampires survive night to night upholding the Masquerade and squabble with each other. Werewolves run around commiting mass murder. What do sorcerers do? Are they lackeys to the Mages, a la ghoul game? Are they fighting against the Mages to gain avatars of their own?<br /> <br /> <br /> Your post kinda got eaten here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never thought that sorcerors would be a good fitting for PCs. That &quot;race&quot; of supernaturals are not interesting... At all.<br /> <br /> Acolites, Extraordinary Citizens... That's their purpose. Not exactly lackeys to Mages (thou they could be) like pitiful ghouls, but companions... That are viewed as second class people. Cuz that's how Mages would be see those anyway.<br /> <br /> The XP costs... Would only be to have a notion. NPCs usually grow toghether with the players, so it would be good to keep a tab.<br /> <br /> The real stars of the game would be the Mages... But their acolite could be really good in one single thing... Better even in that single thing than the Mages themselves. Maybe their acolite is REALLY good in seeing the future... Maybe he is a great scryer for seeing distant places, maybe he is a great mind reader... Perhaps the guy can make and mantain all the portals of a chapel. But they only do that one thing. Those individuals however, could be VERY useful on cabals of Mages, and so they could be highly valuable assets. That would also give an incentive to the Mages to keep sleepers as students, as disciples. Most cabals, would probably have the Mages at the top of it, and a few sleepers being educated to become limited sorcerors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T05:49:41-08:00","id":1039388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039219-why-i-hate-sorcerers-rules-or-why-they-don-t-fit-in-mage?p=1039335#post1039335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12880\" data-vbnamecard=\"12880\">Karlgust</a><br /> \u200bI think the main problem you are having is that WoD is a kitchen sink setting. That means that the stories you tell with it will be set in a world that has a whole lot of stuff in it. There are more than a dozen varieties of vampires. There are more than twenty kinds of magic. There are ten million billion shapeshifter types. And that means that there are a lot of stories you can tell. It means that you can tell a story that revolves around any one of those unique types of vampires, or one that involves people using any of those kinds of magic. But there are also stories you cannot tell. You can't tell a story where, like in Lightbringer, there are strict rules of magic and everyone follows them. You can't tell a story where anyone is particularly surprised that they don't recognize some new shapeshifting monster, because there are so many of those things that hopping around that no one expects to be able to identify them all. In short, you can't tell a story where <i>uniqueness is unique</i>. Nor can you tell a story where the edges of things are well defined, because there are too many edges to define.<br /> <br /> &quot;Sorcery is static magic&quot; is a bullshit line meant to explain why vampires and werewolves don't explode in a cloud of paradox, because the world as Mage writers wrote it doesn't allow the existence of vampires and werewolves. It's a cludge meant to rectify the glaring error of world building. And it's a cludge that made WoD more of a kitchen sink than it was before. Personally, I like reductionist fantasy more than kitchen sink and would cut the sorcerers entirely given the chance.</div> </div> </div> </div>However the sun vulnerability and blood dependence and the other crap could just be Paradox Flaws(pale, no life signs) Burns (Sun) and Quiet (the Beast/the old vampires wanna eat my soul) while the blood is your daily fuel to prevent pattern bleeding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T06:58:11-08:00","id":1039403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039219-why-i-hate-sorcerers-rules-or-why-they-don-t-fit-in-mage?p=1039388#post1039388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> However the sun vulnerability and blood dependence and the other crap could just be Paradox Flaws(pale, no life signs) Burns (Sun) and Quiet (the Beast/the old vampires wanna eat my soul) while the blood is your daily fuel to prevent pattern bleeding.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, great ideas!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T07:10:17-08:00","id":1039409,"title":"","content":"Nice &quot;this is the reason I hate it, and why you all should hate it too&quot; speech you've got there.<br /> <br /> I honestly think you're being overly dismissive about the expansive nature of the content.<br /> <br /> Personally, I love the metaplot. I love the idea of a game which isn't stagnant, which has a history to it which changes with the time. I love that what was a new event for players 10 years ago can be looked upon as history for new players today. It gives the world some weight, makes it feel alive.<br /> Also, I think all these extra options help enrich the environment of the game. Sure trying to include everything at once sacrifices focus, but that was the point of them. I don't think WW ever expected storytellers to look through all their books and decide what role every single Fera, Craft, Clan, etc would take in their story, rather they were trying to fill in a few of the games, give illustrations around the dark corners.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing. If mage was just Traditions and Technocracy, you have yourself a great number of cultures which are ignored or simply absorbed into the others. The Islamic batini would just be a sect of the chorus, losing their unique Arabian focus. Similarly kopa Loa would just be another example of &quot;everything third world's a dreamspeaker&quot;.<br /> What's good about the crafts is it demonstrates that not every magic user has to be a tradition, and indeed new crafts can spring up in areas where belief is strong.<br /> <br /> Not everything fits into a neat little bubble, and just because stories like Traditions vs Technocracy are easy to understand does not mean they are the only story worth adhearing to.<br /> <br /> The Sorcerer fills an important niche, they are the humans who were left behind, the sleepers who did not have the great eppiphay that, for all intents and purposes, is beyond anyone's control. But they still believe, they still make up the zeitgeist and are able to use the gaps in the consensus to their advantage.<br /> While mages recreate reality within their own image, it is the sorcerors who ensure magic is a constant part of reality.<br /> That's why there's been an upsurge of Extrordinary citizens, it's because the technocracy have been winning. Their paradigm has become the dominant one and as such becoming an extraordinary citizen is easier than ever.<br /> The sorcerors are become of hope for the traditions, for as long as they are around, able to keep their practices a part of static reality, magick will never truly die.<br /> While the traditions may fight to protect the sleepers, it is the sorcerors who truly preserve the arts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T08:15:26-08:00","id":1039421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039219-why-i-hate-sorcerers-rules-or-why-they-don-t-fit-in-mage?p=1039409#post1039409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the thing. If mage was just Traditions and Technocracy, you have yourself a great number of cultures which are ignored or simply absorbed into the others. The Islamic batini would just be a sect of the chorus, losing their unique Arabian focus. Similarly kopa Loa would just be another example of &quot;everything third world's a dreamspeaker&quot;.<br /> What's good about the crafts is it demonstrates that not every magic user has to be a tradition, and indeed new crafts can spring up in areas where belief is strong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Counter argument: this waters down the setting and diminishes the importance of every group. Once you've added the Crafts, the Traditions have gone down from a major threat the Technocracy cares about to one of the many terrorist organisations.<br /> Second counter argument: the magical traditions Crafts represent are too minor to warrant a separate faction. Kopa Loei represent hawaian shamans and according to the wiki have 15-30 members. Why does this school club need to be special snowflakes who stand their ground alone in the fight against the forces of reason?<br /> <br /> Saying that every shaman is a dreamspeaker is <i>okay.</i> In fact - that's the entire point. Various tribal shamans united under a broad umbrella of dreamspeakers. Various monotheists united under a broad umbrella of Celestial Chorus. It's an anti-technocratic alliance. So long as you have a freedom to say &quot;my character is a Tuvan shaman who interacts with spirits by throat singing&quot; - you don't need an entire faction of Tuvan throat singers. You just say that they are members of a dreamspeaker faction of the Traditions and call it a day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T08:33:11-08:00","id":1039426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039219-why-i-hate-sorcerers-rules-or-why-they-don-t-fit-in-mage?p=1039421#post1039421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Counter argument: this waters down the setting and diminishes the importance of every group. Once you've added the Crafts, the Traditions have gone down from a major threat the Technocracy cares about to one of the many terrorist organisations.<br /> Second counter argument: the magical traditions Crafts represent are too minor to warrant a separate faction. Kopa Loei represent hawaian shamans and according to the wiki have 15-30 members. Why does this school club need to be special snowflakes who stand their ground alone in the fight against the forces of reason?<br /> <br /> Saying that every shaman is a dreamspeaker is <i>okay.</i> In fact - that's the entire point. Various tribal shamans united under a broad umbrella of dreamspeakers. Various monotheists united under a broad umbrella of Celestial Chorus. It's an anti-technocratic alliance. So long as you have a freedom to say &quot;my character is a Tuvan shaman who interacts with spirits by throat singing&quot; - you don't need an entire faction of Tuvan throat singers. You just say that they are members of a dreamspeaker faction of the Traditions and call it a day.</div> </div> </div> </div>Side argument and honest questions about an individual problem with the game's premise: how is anyone that actually ascribes to a real life practice of beliefs a mage, when the game is about reality warping to meet an individual's vision above all else? Why would these people be warping reality? I can't help but think that this would go against some sort of value system and bring similar concerns of hubris from across cultures. Mages are more the people about whom cautionary tales are told, not the people who run things and set standards for everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T08:44:13-08:00","id":1039436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039219-why-i-hate-sorcerers-rules-or-why-they-don-t-fit-in-mage?p=1039426#post1039426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Side argument and honest questions about an individual problem with the game's premise: how is anyone that actually ascribes to a real life practice of beliefs a mage, when the game is about reality warping to meet an individual's vision above all else? Why would these people be warping reality? I can't help but think that this would go against some sort of value system and bring similar concerns of hubris from across cultures. Mages are more the people about whom cautionary tales are told, not the people who run things and set standards for everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well we know that Phil &quot;Satyros&quot; Brucato genuinely believes in magic and has gone on record saying that he doesn't want playable Nephandi because he doesn't want players turning evil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T09:02:53-08:00","id":1039442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039219-why-i-hate-sorcerers-rules-or-why-they-don-t-fit-in-mage?p=1039426#post1039426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Side argument and honest questions about an individual problem with the game's premise: how is anyone that actually ascribes to a real life practice of beliefs a mage, when the game is about reality warping to meet an individual's vision above all else? Why would these people be warping reality? I can't help but think that this would go against some sort of value system and bring similar concerns of hubris from across cultures. Mages are more the people about whom cautionary tales are told, not the people who run things and set standards for everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, that's EXACTLY what ALL Mages do.<br /> <br /> Mages feel themselves the top of the evolutionary chain... While vampires may believe they are better than puny mortals, werewolves believe they are chosen to be above humans and changelling believing they are a special breed... None of those feel HUMANS. They feel themselves as <u>another race</u>, some think they are cursed, some that they are blessed. They may cling to some trace of humanity, but they know they aren't humans.<br /> <br /> Mages, on the other hand, see themselves as THE BEST of human kind. Therefore, they feel they are the ones that should guide the &quot;blinded sleepers/masses&quot;.<br /> <br /> Mages know better. Mages know what's good for you and what's not better than YOU. That holds true for the Union, for the Traditions, for crafts.<br /> <br /> The best the poor rabble can expect from those special iluminated souls, is that they don't give a damn about you. If that Monk just stay in his mountain meditating, that's the best outcome a Mage can offer you.<br /> <br /> Because if not, he will tell you that you can't make sacrifices for the spirits of the harvest. You have to pile rocks pointing to Orion to do that. And if you don't, they'll curse you. Or you have to pray to the one, and if you use teas and cristals in some supersticious attempt of healing a disease, they'll toast you. Or, if you keep insisting that faeries are real, they'll send you to room 101.<br /> <br /> That's actually what happens when different groups get toghether. What happened when the Eutanatoi and Akasha met each other?<br /> -&quot;You're wrong! Change your insane ways or you'll be sorry!&quot;<br /> -&quot;No, you're wrong! Change your insane ways or YOU will be sorry!&quot;<br /> And that's basically the history of Mages... On rare occasions would they sit toghether and say &quot;well, that's an interesting point of view, but what do you think about that other one...&quot;<br /> <br /> When you awake and apply to one Hermetic House, they don't wanna hear rubbish about &quot;psychodelic drugs&quot;. They'll teach you what they share. If you go to an Akashic Temple, they'll kick your butt if you say that &quot;some people should be removed for the betterment of all&quot; like the Euthanatos.<br /> <br /> You'll only adhere to one of those &quot;clubs&quot; if you follow the stream. From time to time, alliances will be formed, and schisms will happen. Thats how you end up with the once proud Wu Lungs as part of the Akashics, or House Ex Miscelania rises amongst hermetics.<br /> <br /> You could say that the Traditions are each one of them a set of Traditions themselves, United by political convenience under some convergency points. But they are already higly diverse; so, other than a few major crafts, like the Batini or Taftani, the rest SHOULD be just some fringe secret groups. The rest are in one of the Traditions are semi independent sub groups (like ngoma in the Dreamspeakers, madzimbwabe in the Eutanothos, Eu Lung in the Akashic and so on).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T09:04:08-08:00","id":1039445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039219-why-i-hate-sorcerers-rules-or-why-they-don-t-fit-in-mage?p=1039421#post1039421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Counter argument: this waters down the setting and diminishes the importance of every group. Once you've added the Crafts, the Traditions have gone down from a major threat the Technocracy cares about to one of the many terrorist organisations.<br /> Second counter argument: the magical traditions Crafts represent are too minor to warrant a separate faction. Kopa Loei represent hawaian shamans and according to the wiki have 15-30 members. Why does this school club need to be special snowflakes who stand their ground alone in the fight against the forces of reason?<br /> <br /> Saying that every shaman is a dreamspeaker is <i>okay.</i> In fact - that's the entire point. Various tribal shamans united under a broad umbrella of dreamspeakers. Various monotheists united under a broad umbrella of Celestial Chorus. It's an anti-technocratic alliance. So long as you have a freedom to say &quot;my character is a Tuvan shaman who interacts with spirits by throat singing&quot; - you don't need an entire faction of Tuvan throat singers. You just say that they are members of a dreamspeaker faction of the Traditions and call it a day.</div> </div> </div> </div>The main difference between the Technocracy and the Mages are that the mages do not share a consistent ideology on how magic should work. They may argue a hell of a lot, and indeed may become outright tyrannical in the way they press their practices. But unlike the Technocracy, for the most part they recognise that enforcing one overriding consensus does more harm to their cause than good. And while the Technocracy has unity on their side, they lack in versatility.<br /> <br /> Your insistence on Tradition conformity is, therefore, a very technocratic argument. No doubt there are several mages that have put forth similar viewpoints. But let us not forget, the Traditions are a Hermetic idea, and it's all very well and good touting the benefits of conformity and speaking in a united voice when it's your own language that become the shared language. The Dreamspeakers were grouped together because the Hermetics had a superficial view of them. Lumping them together hundreds of different tribes with views ranging in compatibility from similar enough to outright contradictory. Why did they do this? Because partially because the Hermetics didn't recognise their differences, &quot;Oh, another Shaman, take them to the Dreamspeaker table&quot;, others considered their tribes so small and secular that their individuality didn't really matter all that much in the grand scheme of things.<br /> <br /> For the dreamspeakers, this was an insult, and is the main reason why they remain the most aloof of the Council of Nine. However, as the Ascension war raged on, there are some shamans that saw a benefit in their superficial union. Now many of them band together for survival, not our of shared belief, but so the Council will take their requests more seriously. As such, unlike the Hermetics or the Choristors, there is no central governance for the Dreamspeakers, many of them act alone or in small tribes, but will emphasise a shared comoradere, and a willingness to aid one another in the face of greater threats, including the Hubris of the Council.<br /> <br /> However, there are groups that rejected the Hermetic's attempts at amalgamation outright. For them, their pride was so great that to consider others on equal footing was tantamount to betrayal of their own ways. These are the conservative few who cling to their ideas and consider the Tradition's fight as not their own.<br /> Why do they exist? Because this attitude is all too human. Pride creates such rifts, and that is where the crafts are forged.<br /> <br /> So you can say every Shaman is a Dreamspeaker, but then you'd be simplifying what is a very big problem with humanity. Pride and an stubborn adherence to what we are already used to.<br /> <br /> <br /> But that is the main thing, the Traditions are more coordinated than the crafts. For the most part the crafts are pretty isolated, hidden within the far corners of the globe keeping mostly to themselves. I doubt the technocracy even acknowledges them at all, let alone considers them worthy of discussion.<br /> My guess is that most Technocrats don't eve know there's a difference. All mages are part of this Tradition alliance. But that's of course assuming these technocrats in particular are briefed on how Mages operate.<br /> Some Technocrats won't even consider such distinctions outside of &quot;categorise their ways to make it easier to fight them.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, Mage isn't a story, it's a setting. It's a play set filled with toys. It's up to us to make games with them. You don't need to use every toy in the box, but they are there if you have the interest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T09:17:56-08:00","id":1039452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039219-why-i-hate-sorcerers-rules-or-why-they-don-t-fit-in-mage?p=1039436#post1039436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well we know that Phil &quot;Satyros&quot; Brucato genuinely believes in magic and has gone on record saying that he doesn't want playable Nephandi because he doesn't want players turning evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow. He must <b><i>hate</i></b> the Shadow play of Wraith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T10:26:46-08:00","id":1039490,"title":"","content":"Oops, now I realized one thing that may be causing confusion: the title of the thread.<br /> <br /> So, to correct it: &quot;Why they don't fit in Mage&quot;, what I really wanted to say was &quot;Why I think the rules for their powers don't fit in Mage&quot;.<br /> <br /> Now I get it some people objections... I actually think that the idea of those &quot;sleepwalkers&quot; are a great adition to Mage, but I don't like their thaumaturgical-like powers...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T10:53:35-08:00","id":1039511,"title":"","content":"How about this:<br /> <br /> Each sorceror MUST have an occultism-like knowledge... That's a skill that represents their grasp of their personal <u>paradigm</u>.<br /> <br /> So, for example:<br /> <br /> Personal Science (Etherite)<br /> Consensual Science (Technocratic)<br /> Virtuality (VA)<br /> Witchcraft (Verbena)<br /> High Arts (Hermetic)<br /> Do (Akashic)<br /> Celestial (CC)<br /> Balance (Batini)<br /> <br /> And so on; it's a variation of Occultism (so the char won't have both), but with a paradigm lenses.<br /> <br /> That skill will determine the maximum level of the effects the sorceror can have, and to have access to higher level effects, he must have at least one effect of the previous level. If you wanna, you can make it so that whatnever the sorceror increases one point in that skill, he gains a new effect of the same level.<br /> <br /> And yes, one could learn more than one Paradigm, if they spend the XP for it (and role play it)<br /> <br /> How does he buy the effects: any effect is a separate fixed &quot;power&quot;. The level of the effect is determined by the highest level of Sphere on it, so for example:<br /> <br /> Steel Skin (Life 4, Matter 2) <br /> <br /> Is a level 4 effect.<br /> <br /> Mind Scan (Corr 1, Mind 1)<br /> <br /> Is a level 1 effect.<br /> <br /> The costs would be, level of the effect x2 in XP. So:<br /> <br /> Level 1 - 2 XP<br /> Level 2 - 4 XP<br /> Level 3 - 6 XP<br /> Level 4 - 8 XP<br /> Level 5 - 10 XP.<br /> <br /> Those prices are adjustable as you see fit. If you wanna more powerful sorcerors, make costs be 1 XP/lvl. If wanna them with very few powers, make 3XP/lvl or more.<br /> <br /> Casting: effects have two categories: spells (fast and dirty) and rituals (low and powerful). Some spells also have a ritual version (and vice versa), but they count as two different effects, and must be learned apart.<br /> <br /> For Spells: Wits+Paradigm Skill<br /> For Rituals: Inteligence+Paradigm Skill.<br /> <br /> Number of successes: double the requirements for mages. For damage, each success does only one damage, +1 if it is Forces, and so on.<br /> <br /> If that's not for your liking, roll just their Paradigm Skill and deal the same way as Arete rolls.<br /> <br /> Paradox: if anyone care to help me here I would appreciate. I'm thinking that instead of Paradox, they could receive &quot;Desbelief&quot;, and that thing would cause effects to malfunction or not working at all from time to time.<br /> <br /> How's that now?<br /> <br /> PS: mind you, if you like the sorcerors as they are, it's fine. It's just that for me, is not to my liking, so I really would like to make a new way that would be functional, any idea would be helpful","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T12:29:55-08:00","id":1039550,"title":"","content":"I think Proximi do the table scraps of enlightenment thing better than Sorcerers. I wish there was a better connection between sorcery, abilities in general and Mage mechanics but I don't in theory have a problem with the existance of non Mage magicians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T12:41:24-08:00","id":1039558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039219-why-i-hate-sorcerers-rules-or-why-they-don-t-fit-in-mage?p=1039550#post1039550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Proximi do the table scraps of enlightenment thing better than Sorcerers. I wish there was a better connection between sorcery, abilities in general and Mage mechanics but I don't in theory have a problem with the existance of non Mage magicians.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't either, actually I like the concept, I just saw now that the tittle were ambiguous and misleading, what meant were for the mechanics they made for sorcerors, that's what I don't think that fits","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T12:55:51-08:00","id":1039566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039219-why-i-hate-sorcerers-rules-or-why-they-don-t-fit-in-mage?p=1039452#post1039452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow. He must <b><i>hate</i></b> the Shadow play of Wraith.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure Satyros likes Shadow play in Wraith, and dislikes people lying about what he said. His feelings on playing Nephandi is on page 224 of M20. It doesn't say that playing Nephandi makes you evil (the closest thing he says about that is that role-playing such dark characters can have a negative impact on you, and thus should be done with extreme care).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039219-why-i-hate-sorcerers-rules-or-why-they-don-t-fit-in-mage?p=1039490#post1039490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually think that the idea of those &quot;sleepwalkers&quot; are a great adition to Mage, but I don't like their thaumaturgical-like powers...</div> </div> </div> </div>Their powers should be like Thaumaturgy.<br /> <br /> In setting Thaumaturgy is based on Sorcerer Paths, so Sorcerer Paths need to look like Thaumaturgy for that to make any sense. Remember, the Tremere are fallen Hermetics who turned their magic into Thaumaturgy using their greater proficiency with Sorcerer Paths than dynamic magic compared to other Houses.<br /> <br /> If Thaumaturgy and Sorcery look nothing alike, it doesn't make any sense with the setting as written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T15:52:02-08:00","id":1039638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039219-why-i-hate-sorcerers-rules-or-why-they-don-t-fit-in-mage?p=1039357#post1039357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">no run for secret albino Vietnamise cultists or Cambodjan cannibals or chinese shemales to have that unique power, that exclusive thaumaturgical line, oh, the only ones that have access to the abyss mysticism so I wanna split their skulls to steal it. <br /> <br /> No. All those freaks will have the same spheres as anybody else.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:red\">People with Albinoism and trans women are real groups of people, and calling them freaks is against the forum rules. The term &quot;shemale&quot; in particular is a slur. I'm going to give you a warning because this is your first offense, but a post like this would normally get you a suspension for at least a week.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T16:14:51-08:00","id":1039655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039219-why-i-hate-sorcerers-rules-or-why-they-don-t-fit-in-mage?p=1039638#post1039638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:red\">People with Albinoism and trans women are real groups of people, and calling them freaks is against the forum rules. The term &amp;quot;shemale&amp;quot; in particular is a slur. I'm going to give you a warning because this is your first offense, but a post like this would normally get you a suspension for at least a week.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Shemale&quot; is the only term I know in english, I didn't even knew it were offensive. The term &quot;freaks&quot; was about the ultra peculiar nonsensical groups (infernalist transex, underground albino group). I mean, whats the purpose of a group of transex (or whatever the non offensive word for that) or a sect of exclusively albinos? Note that I also included the cambojan infernalist cannibals. I didn't meant they were freaks for being abinos or transex, but for being groups composed of simply unusual conditions. Hey, people should be offended that they have a group of transex that are ALL INFERNALISTS. And, while I can agree that transex can be mages, and can also be infernalists in the game... An entire group? Really? Or: how many albinos are there in the world? Ok, so I would aassume that there wouldnt be many albino Mages too. So, having a group of only THAT. It feels like the only purpose of such groups are to be weird, to be different. It's like making a group with only people mutilated. Whats the purpose of that? Its only to make such groups look like... Freaks. That's my critic, and that's what I meant. I think those ideas have a bad taste about 'em.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T16:39:57-08:00","id":1039673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039219-why-i-hate-sorcerers-rules-or-why-they-don-t-fit-in-mage?p=1039566#post1039566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their powers should be like Thaumaturgy.<br /> <br /> In setting Thaumaturgy is based on Sorcerer Paths, so Sorcerer Paths need to look like Thaumaturgy for that to make any sense. Remember, the Tremere are fallen Hermetics who turned their magic into Thaumaturgy using their greater proficiency with Sorcerer Paths than dynamic magic compared to other Houses.<br /> <br /> If Thaumaturgy and Sorcery look nothing alike, it doesn't make any sense with the setting as written.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This isn't actually a supported. I mean it MAKE more sense but everyone gets upset when you say Tremere was just a Sorcerer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T16:50:37-08:00","id":1039682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039219-why-i-hate-sorcerers-rules-or-why-they-don-t-fit-in-mage?p=1039566#post1039566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their powers should be like Thaumaturgy.<br /> <br /> In setting Thaumaturgy is based on Sorcerer Paths, so Sorcerer Paths need to look like Thaumaturgy for that to make any sense. Remember, the Tremere are fallen Hermetics who turned their magic into Thaumaturgy using their greater proficiency with Sorcerer Paths than dynamic magic compared to other Houses.<br /> <br /> If Thaumaturgy and Sorcery look nothing alike, it doesn't make any sense with the setting as written.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never knew the Tremere were mostly sorcerors; as far as I know, they were awaken. Besides, Thaumaturgy is a discipline, so it makes sense that it has the disciples structure (that is very different from Garou gifts for example). <br /> But sorcery is a type of limitated &quot;true magik&quot;. It should be the SAME &quot;k&quot; Magic as Mages, but without the elastic capacity of &quot;real true&quot; magik. But, in theory, the source of those powers is the same - the human Avatar.<br /> <br /> Unlike thaumaturgy that have as the source of their power their cursed blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T17:06:19-08:00","id":1039691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039219-why-i-hate-sorcerers-rules-or-why-they-don-t-fit-in-mage?p=1039682#post1039682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I never knew the Tremere were mostly sorcerors; as far as I know, they were awaken. Besides, Thaumaturgy is a discipline, so it makes sense that it has the disciples structure (that is very different from Garou gifts for example). <br /> But sorcery is a type of limitated &amp;quot;true magik&amp;quot;. It should be the SAME &amp;quot;k&amp;quot; Magic as Mages, but without the elastic capacity of &amp;quot;real true&amp;quot; magik. But, in theory, the source of those powers is the same - the human Avatar.<br /> <br /> Unlike thaumaturgy that have as the source of their power their cursed blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once you go vamp, the avatar leaves. I suppose they resorted to sorcery in order to try and reclaim what power they once had.<br /> <br /> Also, you insistence that thaumaturgy and sorcery should be entirely separate methods is pretty unfounded.<br /> Sorcerers are not Mages by definition. Their sleeping avatar is not the source of their power, it cannot be. It can't hold or interact with quintessence, and the world will not change because of what a sorcerer believes. They make changes based on pre-existing parameters.<br /> <br /> It works the other way around. While a Mage's practices work because they believe it will work, a sorcerer believes it will work because it does work.<br /> <br /> Anyone could do what a sorcerer does in theory, but it requires a great deal of practice, understanding, and sheer force of will to drive it home.<br /> <br /> In theory, a sorcerer would be able to do things in another's paradigm just as well, but because the paths require very specific activity and mindsets to work, most sorcerers stick to what's familiar. A priest will leave the science to the scientists and focus on their holy books, a witch will leave the Egyptian symbols alone, preferring to stick with their runes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T17:38:03-08:00","id":1039710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039219-why-i-hate-sorcerers-rules-or-why-they-don-t-fit-in-mage?p=1039638#post1039638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:red\">People with Albinoism and trans women are real groups of people, and calling them freaks is against the forum rules. The term &quot;shemale&quot; in particular is a slur. I'm going to give you a warning because this is your first offense, but a post like this would normally get you a suspension for at least a week.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>For what it's worth I actually support this decision <br /> <br /> I don't think English is karlgust's first language and that his words, while perhaps offensive to some, were not intended to be so.<br /> <br /> Is it not wise and merciful to spare those who do not know better the punishment for the crime they have committed? (no offence karlgust)<br /> <br /> Not that you need to be asked this question Charlaquin, I'm just putting it out there for others on the forum who might disagree with your decision.<br /> <br /> I actually think that all the posts in this thread should be left up too, I went back and read them one by one after all and I think this discussion has educational value, not in spite of the words that made you step in and moderate but BECAUSE of them and the statements that followed them.<br /> <br /> Call me naive and idealistic but I actually think the forum can be a place of enlightened idea sharing and tolerance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T17:42:52-08:00","id":1039712,"title":"","content":"Where the hell is dreamweaver, someone call him, or her, or xer in here (I think he's male). He made a great set of rules for sorcerery, it needed work (by his own admission) but it was damn good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T18:41:23-08:00","id":1039732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039219-why-i-hate-sorcerers-rules-or-why-they-don-t-fit-in-mage?p=1039691#post1039691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Once you go vamp, the avatar leaves. I suppose they resorted to sorcery in order to try and reclaim what power they once had.<br /> <br /> Also, you insistence that thaumaturgy and sorcery should be entirely separate methods is pretty unfounded.<br /> Sorcerers are not Mages by definition. Their sleeping avatar is not the source of their power, it cannot be. It can't hold or interact with quintessence, and the world will not change because of what a sorcerer believes. They make changes based on pre-existing parameters.<br /> <br /> It works the other way around. While a Mage's practices work because they believe it will work, a sorcerer believes it will work because it does work.<br /> <br /> Anyone could do what a sorcerer does in theory, but it requires a great deal of practice, understanding, and sheer force of will to drive it home.<br /> <br /> In theory, a sorcerer would be able to do things in another's paradigm just as well, but because the paths require very specific activity and mindsets to work, most sorcerers stick to what's familiar. A priest will leave the science to the scientists and focus on their holy books, a witch will leave the Egyptian symbols alone, preferring to stick with their runes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. So, perhaps it is thaumaturgy that is out of place. Ill explain.<br /> <br /> Now, I do agree with you, that sorcery is not connected to belief <i>per se</i>. I think you're right.<br /> <br /> In fact, it is connected to CONSENSUS. Indeed, sorcerers can do what they do... Because <u>reality allows them to</u>.<br /> <br /> But, of course a prist sorceror is not working in the technocratic Consensus. But he is working within the Consensus of the Celestial Chorus. Or, a shaman sorceror is working with the &quot;Consensus&quot; of the Dreamspeakers, so to say.<br /> <br /> Be that as it may, the sorcerors can do what they do, because there ARE paradigms that ALLOW them to do that... Because those paradigms <i>shape</i> the reality, realities that those sorcerors can deal with (summoning angels for a priest sorcer is like turning a TV on to us).<br /> <br /> Therefore, they arent totally cut off from the chains f Paradigm.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And it MUST be connected to Paradigm... Otherwise, sorcerors would be limited by CONSENSUS alone (after all, they can only do what reality allows them to do). That would mean that priests wouldn't be able to use their sorcery outside the Celestial Chorus chantry.<br /> <br /> But, once again, RAW just makes their powers a cool collection of random stuff. With no connection with the technocrat consensus, or the &quot;hermetic Consensus&quot; etc<br /> <br /> EDIT 2: isn't Consensus created by the sleepers AVATARS? So, it isn't totally ilogical to think that sorcerors use their avatars in a &quot;sleepwalking&quot; mode of sorts. Anyway, they either work upon the boundaries of Consensus, or they can make their sleeping Avatars have &quot;vivid dreams&quot;. Either way, they must work under the boundaries of Paradigm... So, I would expect them to be able to do what the Mages with the same paradigm can - only in more limited ways","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","user":"Karlgust","date":". 01-28-2017, 09:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T18:44:05-08:00","id":1039734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039219-why-i-hate-sorcerers-rules-or-why-they-don-t-fit-in-mage?p=1039732#post1039732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fair enough. So, perhaps it is thaumaturgy that is out of place. Ill explain.<br /> <br /> Now, I do agree with you, that sorcery is not connected to belief <i>per se</i>. I think you're right.<br /> <br /> In fact, it is connected to CONSENSUS. Indeed, sorcerers can do what they do... Because <u>reality allows them to</u>.<br /> <br /> But, of course a prist sorceror is not working in the technocratic Consensus. But he is working within the Consensus of the Celestial Chorus. Or, a shaman sorceror is working with the &amp;quot;Consensus&amp;quot; of the Dreamspeakers, so to say.<br /> <br /> Be that as it may, the sorcerors can do what they do, because there ARE paradigms that ALLOW them to do that... Because those paradigms <i>shape</i> the reality, realities that those sorcerors can deal with (summoning angels for a priest sorcer is like turning a TV on to us).<br /> <br /> Therefore, they arent totally cut off from the chains f Paradigm.</div> </div> </div> </div>But they are cut off from the spheres, from quintessence, and thus from paradox. Obscenely vulgar magic is usually not on the table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T19:21:59-08:00","id":1039748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039219-why-i-hate-sorcerers-rules-or-why-they-don-t-fit-in-mage?p=1039673#post1039673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't actually a supported. I mean it MAKE more sense but everyone gets upset when you say Tremere was just a Sorcerer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure it's supported. I didn't say Tremere wasn't a mage (that's not supported at all, it especially doesn't make sense as Tremere himself was known to be a master of Certamen and frequently used it to get his way in Hermetic politics), but there's lots of support for the idea that the Tremere as a House were more reliant on Sorcerers than the others (which is a hold over from Ars Magica and all, but it's still there in places).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039219-why-i-hate-sorcerers-rules-or-why-they-don-t-fit-in-mage?p=1039682#post1039682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides, Thaumaturgy is a discipline, so it makes sense that it has the disciples structure (that is very different from Garou gifts for example).</div> </div> </div> </div>Thaumaturgy has a number of key exceptions to the way most Disciplines work though.<br /> <br /> Ultimately though, you seem to be extremely invested in the mechanical structure of this as if it was an in-character point of debate. Sorcerers don't sit around with vampires to discuss how if you read the rulebooks of the game, Hellfire and Path of the Levinbolt are really similar.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But sorcery is a type of limitated &quot;true magik&quot;. </div> </div> </div>But it explicitly in the books is not. Sorcery is in the books more like Disciplines, just like the rest of the things under the Numina umbrella. Numina being a number of supernatural powers that under the right conditions allow humans (and sometimes not just humans) to use them rather than having to be supernaturals that are fueling some sort of innate/learned power tied to the nature of that supernatural creature.<br /> <br /> The whole Numina umbrella works like Disciplines (and a number of other supernatural powers like Arcanoi and Edges). Either you need to accept that in the WoD this type of power is the easiest structure for channeling mystic powers that violate Reality Zones (since they ignore Reality Zones in general), or not get focused on the mechanical constructs as anything more than abstractions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unlike thaumaturgy that have as the source of their power their cursed blood. </div> </div> </div>Different sources of power doesn't explain why they shouldn't have similar structures.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039219-why-i-hate-sorcerers-rules-or-why-they-don-t-fit-in-mage?p=1039732#post1039732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, it is connected to CONSENSUS. Indeed, sorcerers can do what they do... Because <u>reality allows them to</u>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reality and Consensus aren't the same thing. A linear shaman using Sorcerer paths for their magic that travels to the Umbra is free from Consensus but not reality, and their magic doesn't change.<br /> <br /> Reality allows Sorcerers <b>despite</b> Consensus.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T20:37:32-08:00","id":1039792,"title":"","content":"The fact that Numina exist is one of the many pieces of evidence that there is a fundamental Reality in cWoD outside of the Consensus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T22:14:59-08:00","id":1039823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039219-why-i-hate-sorcerers-rules-or-why-they-don-t-fit-in-mage?p=1039734#post1039734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But they are cut off from the spheres, from quintessence, and thus from paradox. Obscenely vulgar magic is usually not on the table.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would agree with you, sorcerors sholdn't be able to do Vulgar Magic; but that would invalidate both thaumaturgy AND most of the sorcery paths...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T22:24:14-08:00","id":1039827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039219-why-i-hate-sorcerers-rules-or-why-they-don-t-fit-in-mage?p=1039748#post1039748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure it's supported. I didn't say Tremere wasn't a mage (that's not supported at all, it especially doesn't make sense as Tremere himself was known to be a master of Certamen and frequently used it to get his way in Hermetic politics), but there's lots of support for the idea that the Tremere as a House were more reliant on Sorcerers than the others (which is a hold over from Ars Magica and all, but it's still there in places).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Thaumaturgy has a number of key exceptions to the way most Disciplines work though.<br /> <br /> Ultimately though, you seem to be extremely invested in the mechanical structure of this as if it was an in-character point of debate. Sorcerers don't sit around with vampires to discuss how if you read the rulebooks of the game, Hellfire and Path of the Levinbolt are really similar.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But it explicitly in the books is not. Sorcery is in the books more like Disciplines, just like the rest of the things under the Numina umbrella. Numina being a number of supernatural powers that under the right conditions allow humans (and sometimes not just humans) to use them rather than having to be supernaturals that are fueling some sort of innate/learned power tied to the nature of that supernatural creature.<br /> <br /> The whole Numina umbrella works like Disciplines (and a number of other supernatural powers like Arcanoi and Edges). Either you need to accept that in the WoD this type of power is the easiest structure for channeling mystic powers that violate Reality Zones (since they ignore Reality Zones in general), or not get focused on the mechanical constructs as anything more than abstractions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Different sources of power doesn't explain why they shouldn't have similar structures.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Reality and Consensus aren't the same thing. A linear shaman using Sorcerer paths for their magic that travels to the Umbra is free from Consensus but not reality, and their magic doesn't change.<br /> <br /> Reality allows Sorcerers <b>despite</b> Consensus.</div> </div> </div> </div>In that case, their power flows by their sleeping avatars.<br /> <br /> In which case that it would make more sense to be more like Mage effects... And not disciplines<br /> <br /> But now, a matter worth of consideration: where do sorcerors take their powers after all? From their sleeping avatars? Or from... Something else?<br /> <br /> Numina could just as easily be a &quot;Sleepwalking&quot; manifestation of a sleeper's Avatar. No one knows","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T23:22:08-08:00","id":1039847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zennis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039219-why-i-hate-sorcerers-rules-or-why-they-don-t-fit-in-mage?p=1039710#post1039710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it not wise and merciful to spare those who do not know better the punishment for the crime they have committed?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be why I gave them a warning instead of a suspension.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zennis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039219-why-i-hate-sorcerers-rules-or-why-they-don-t-fit-in-mage?p=1039710#post1039710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually think that all the posts in this thread should be left up too, I went back and read them one by one after all and I think this discussion has educational value, not in spite of the words that made you step in and moderate but BECAUSE of them and the statements that followed them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did anyone suggest the posts in the thread should be taken down?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zennis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039219-why-i-hate-sorcerers-rules-or-why-they-don-t-fit-in-mage?p=1039710#post1039710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Call me naive and idealistic but I actually think the forum can be a place of enlightened idea sharing and tolerance.</div> </div> </div> </div>These forums are one of the most positive and tolerant online communities I've seen, so no, I don't think it's naive to say that. I do think it's kind of out of the blue though, was anyone suggesting otherwise?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T00:58:24-08:00","id":1039876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039219-why-i-hate-sorcerers-rules-or-why-they-don-t-fit-in-mage?p=1039847#post1039847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be why I gave them a warning instead of a suspension.<br /> <br /> <br /> Did anyone suggest the posts in the thread should be taken down?<br /> <br /> <br /> These forums are one of the most positive and tolerant online communities I've seen, so no, I don't think it's naive to say that. I do think it's kind of out of the blue though, was anyone suggesting otherwise?</div> </div> </div> </div>Charlaquin, I was complimenting you, did you not get that?<br /> <br /> I'm trying to be positive by speaking out and expressing myself in a supportive way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","user":"Zennis","date":". 01-29-2017, 04:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T01:23:17-08:00","id":1039881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039219-why-i-hate-sorcerers-rules-or-why-they-don-t-fit-in-mage?p=1039827#post1039827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In that case, their power flows by their sleeping avatars.</div> </div> </div> </div>That does not hold with the games as written. Creatures that do not have sleeping avatars have been shown to be capable of using Numina and sometimes specifically Sorcery.<br /> <br /> This means that Sorcery does not rely on having an avatar, but that Sorcery taps into aspects of reality that Consensus either cannot or has not made impossible within the dominant Reality Zones of Earth. Which means it makes no sense to be like Mage effects.<br /> <br /> For example, Fera don't have avatars. It's not part of their spiritual make up. However, some Fera have learned how to access Numina (including Sorcery). This means Sorcery <b>must</b> come from a source other than personal avatars.<br /> <br /> As I already showed, Numina defy Reality Zones.<br /> <br /> While we might not know the exact answer to , &quot;where do Sorcerers take their power from?&quot; any answer has to deal with these considerations. Which means the top contenders are either (1) some supernatural force external to individual Sorcerers actively empowering such things anywhere in existence or (2) all of reality is hardcoded to accept that these work regardless of Consensus or Reality Zones.<br /> <br /> And both have the same basic impact on play, or how these things should be modeled.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T01:28:35-08:00","id":1039882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039219-why-i-hate-sorcerers-rules-or-why-they-don-t-fit-in-mage?p=1039823#post1039823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would agree with you, sorcerors sholdn't be able to do Vulgar Magic; but that would invalidate both thaumaturgy AND most of the sorcery paths...</div> </div> </div> </div>Both versions of Sorcerer mention that doing something like trying to throw a fireball Street Fighter style in a crowded mall would likely fizzle or backfire. (But also warns that STs should use that to prevent crazy, not stifle creative uses.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T04:29:19-08:00","id":1039923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zennis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039219-why-i-hate-sorcerers-rules-or-why-they-don-t-fit-in-mage?p=1039876#post1039876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Charlaquin, I was complimenting you, did you not get that?</div> </div> </div> </div>In fairness to CharChar, I kind of got the impression you were trying to convince them of something, too. I mean, the whole bit mentioning &quot;all the posts should be kept up too&quot; certainly gave that impression. I'm'a guess it's a language barrier thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T04:44:58-08:00","id":1039927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039219-why-i-hate-sorcerers-rules-or-why-they-don-t-fit-in-mage?p=1039923#post1039923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fairness to CharChar, I kind of got the impression you were trying to convince them of something, too. I mean, the whole bit mentioning &amp;quot;all the posts should be kept up too&amp;quot; certainly gave that impression. I'm'a guess it's a language barrier thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see how you might feel that way though the impression you got wasn't accurate, the reason I said what i did is because 'shemale' is such an offensive word that to some, it should be taken down no matter what.<br /> <br /> I actually think this discussion is a good example of someone learning something and i feel that that example looses its validity if we take even part of it off the forum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T08:21:23-08:00","id":1039997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039219-why-i-hate-sorcerers-rules-or-why-they-don-t-fit-in-mage?p=1039882#post1039882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Both versions of Sorcerer mention that doing something like trying to throw a fireball Street Fighter style in a crowded mall would likely fizzle or backfire. (But also warns that STs should use that to prevent crazy, not stifle creative uses.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I interpret that as more of an innate group counterspell ability rather than anything related to the Consensus. I assign one die of counterspell for every one hundred direct mortal witnesses if the direct mortal witnesses have not been explicitly warned to expect magical effects (which I also apply to Changeling Arts, Fera Gifts, Kindred Sorcery, Mage Spheres, etc). It means that supernatural PCs keep to the shadows and avoid showing off in front of crowds (but it still means that supernatural characters can perform 'tricks' in front of crowds if they warn the crowd that 'tricks' will occur).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T08:42:22-08:00","id":1040004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039219-why-i-hate-sorcerers-rules-or-why-they-don-t-fit-in-mage?p=1039882#post1039882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Both versions of Sorcerer mention that doing something like trying to throw a fireball Street Fighter style in a crowded mall would likely fizzle or backfire. (But also warns that STs should use that to prevent crazy, not stifle creative uses.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Clearly you need to be practicing the Shih's Devil Judgment instead of hedge magic if you want your Hadouken. (^VVVVVV^)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T09:00:42-08:00","id":1040018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039219-why-i-hate-sorcerers-rules-or-why-they-don-t-fit-in-mage?p=1039881#post1039881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That does not hold with the games as written. Creatures that do not have sleeping avatars have been shown to be capable of using Numina and sometimes specifically Sorcery.<br /> <br /> This means that Sorcery does not rely on having an avatar, but that Sorcery taps into aspects of reality that Consensus either cannot or has not made impossible within the dominant Reality Zones of Earth. Which means it makes no sense to be like Mage effects.<br /> <br /> For example, Fera don't have avatars. It's not part of their spiritual make up. However, some Fera have learned how to access Numina (including Sorcery). This means Sorcery <b>must</b> come from a source other than personal avatars.<br /> <br /> As I already showed, Numina defy Reality Zones.<br /> <br /> While we might not know the exact answer to , &amp;quot;where do Sorcerers take their power from?&amp;quot; any answer has to deal with these considerations. Which means the top contenders are either (1) some supernatural force external to individual Sorcerers actively empowering such things anywhere in existence or (2) all of reality is hardcoded to accept that these work regardless of Consensus or Reality Zones.<br /> <br /> And both have the same basic impact on play, or how these things should be modeled.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hum... I see. That indeed seems about right than.<br /> <br /> But if so, why cant Mages learn sorcery paths?<br /> <br /> Or is the Avatar &quot;alergic&quot; to static magic?<br /> <br /> And, if that last option is the case, shouldn't Mage ghouls have a ban on learning disciplines? (and the same restrictions for kinfolk Mages to learn gifts or kinain to learn cantrips - althouth there is a lot of discussion about those traits for Mages, but at least ghouls CAN learn disciplines despite the Awakened status)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T09:04:08-08:00","id":1040020,"title":"","content":"Im truly sorry to all, I never knew that the world 'shemale' were so offensive. I thought it were common to use it in spoken english. One of the downsides from learning the language in the internet I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T13:06:01-08:00","id":1040163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039219-why-i-hate-sorcerers-rules-or-why-they-don-t-fit-in-mage?p=1040018#post1040018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if so, why cant Mages learn sorcery paths?<br /> <br /> Or is the Avatar &quot;alergic&quot; to static magic?<br /> <br /> And, if that last option is the case, shouldn't Mage ghouls have a ban on learning disciplines? (and the same restrictions for kinfolk Mages to learn gifts or kinain to learn cantrips - althouth there is a lot of discussion about those traits for Mages, but at least ghouls CAN learn disciplines despite the Awakened status)</div> </div> </div> </div>The books case for mages not being able to learn sorcery is largely a game concern. The authors have been clear that even if a Path might look tempting, it is largely an XP trap for mages. Mastering a Path costs a huge amount of XP, for a few tricks that are Paradox free, compared to what the mage could get with Spheres.<br /> <br /> The in-character explanation is not terribly strong for it. But it is sufficient: once you awake up, you can't go back to sleep. Once a mage has awakened, they have to interact with the world through the lens of a mage. They understand too much of how things really work to try to &quot;dumb it down&quot; and perform Numina magic (except True Faith in most incarnations of it, but TF is weird even for Numina); their enlightened knowledge just has to butt in. The closest a mage can do is pull on the mystic threads that allow Numina, making their magic easier by following the same in-character rules sorcery uses, but it's still dynamic magic in disguise.<br /> <br /> As for &quot;should mages be able to learn other supernatural powers&quot; thing, metaphysically it's questionable once they're in the category of having spiritual/etc. connections like that. But really, the out-of-character point that the amount of expense in learning a Gift for a Kin-mage is so high, it's stupid to even bother.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T13:44:03-08:00","id":1040186,"title":"","content":"The main reason I'd think mages wouldn't go with paths is because the paths have a sort of stigma to them. For Hermetics, the paths are not real magic at all, but a tool to help one gain the right frame of mind to proceed to real magic. Returning to the paths after awakening would be like a cyclist opting to put training wheels back on their bike. It looks silly, and makes them seem less able in the eyes of other mages.<br /> <br /> This view is echoed by many other traditions, though in different ways.<br /> The Choristers that awaken are closer to The One than the others, and as such have a duty to revere The One's power. Returning to Static Magic then may be seen as a rejecting the wisdom of The One in order to stay with what was once familiar, a step backwards.<br /> Ecstatics would not be able to achieve the same high they once did, and would grow less and less satisfied with hedge magic. They may be able to, but it doesn't really do anything for them anymore. Kinda like how once you've watched a HD Television, going back to SD is rather disappointing.<br /> Virtual Adepts would avoid wanting to seem Lame by sticking with standard Bleater style coding. Rep is everything with these guys.<br /> and the Akashics (last example, I promise) would also feel as though they are relying on a crutch if they go back to static magic. Theirs is a solitary journey of constant examining of ones ways and lifestyles. If one is unable to let go of what they hold on to, then they are trapped. Once you've achieved a level of freedom, returning is almost like you've given up trying.<br /> <br /> Also, mechanically speaking, Static Magic is actually pretty annoying to use. You can do barely anything, and it costs WP to use. WP is one of the most often drained resource of all the stats in the games I run. It means you're limited to about five or six spells a week before you just don't have the energy anymore. And for every WP lost, that's another point that can't be used later for those oh so critical automatic successes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T14:34:13-08:00","id":1040215,"title":"","content":"Unless you have Psychic Vampirism, in which WP rains down like mana (playing a character with Psychic Vampirism 4 is really fun, by the way).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 01-29-2017, 05:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T15:08:23-08:00","id":1040233,"title":"","content":"And there's nothing you can do with Psychic Vampirism that you can't do with Mind and Life magic (maybe some Prime depending on how you want to go about it). Heck, Mind should be able to help you restore WP without needing to drain it from other people by creating the mental rest/emotional catharsis that leads to natural WP recovery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T15:48:54-08:00","id":1040254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039219-why-i-hate-sorcerers-rules-or-why-they-don-t-fit-in-mage?p=1040233#post1040233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And there's nothing you can do with Psychic Vampirism that you can't do with Mind and Life magic (maybe some Prime depending on how you want to go about it). Heck, Mind should be able to help you restore WP without needing to drain it from other people by creating the mental rest/emotional catharsis that leads to natural WP recovery.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No. Allowing a mage to absorb WP with sphere magic would basically mean they would never botch anything ever again. Far too overpowered.<br /> <br /> Unless there were a hell of a lot of caveats like Pattern Bleed of the bashing variety, or increase WP roll difficulty or making it vulgar magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 01-29-2017, 06:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T16:12:47-08:00","id":1040266,"title":"","content":"Yes, regaining WP by feeding on sapient creatures is probably the most balanced way to do things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T17:42:11-08:00","id":1040317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039219-why-i-hate-sorcerers-rules-or-why-they-don-t-fit-in-mage?p=1040254#post1040254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. Allowing a mage to absorb WP with sphere magic would basically mean they would never botch anything ever again. Far too overpowered.</div> </div> </div> </div>You still have a maximum amount of WP you can hold.<br /> <br /> And frankly, the idea that it's broken is a pretty non-started argument in Mage. Sphere magic allows a lot of options of questionable &quot;balance.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T18:11:29-08:00","id":1040336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039219-why-i-hate-sorcerers-rules-or-why-they-don-t-fit-in-mage?p=1040317#post1040317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You still have a maximum amount of WP you can hold.<br /> <br /> And frankly, the idea that it's broken is a pretty non-started argument in Mage. Sphere magic allows a lot of options of questionable &quot;balance.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>So how would you limit it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T20:08:33-08:00","id":1040383,"title":"","content":"Never had a reason to. WP has only been a serious concern in situations where the PCs are spending it so fast that taking a turn to try to regain some WP was a turn spent probably dying instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T20:48:53-08:00","id":1040395,"title":"","content":"WP is one of the most valuable resources in cWoD. I doubt that many STs allow characters to regain more than two or three points per session. The ability to regain two or three points per scene is incredibly powerful, which is one of the reasons why PV is so powerful as a Numina.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T21:02:04-08:00","id":1040398,"title":"","content":"And Yet, RAW should allow for Mind 1 (!!!!!) to recover WP. Its just a &quot;simple&quot; mental capacitation... Sorry. Just meditate for 10 minutes, or take that &quot;brain enhancer&quot; drug, and get your mental strenght back up.<br /> <br /> Yep... There is no reason to NOT have Mind 1 making WP regen.<br /> <br /> Not just that: each success would regen 1 WP (maybe you shouldn't allow to use 1 WP to avoid botch, and gain that WP back after the effect. But that would also be valid, in theory)<br /> <br /> If you wanna, you could indeed make pattern bleeding, or turning it Vulgar if you wanna.<br /> <br /> About the questions on sorcerers, thank you all a lot, now I have a much better understanding on them... It has been very informative","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T21:04:34-08:00","id":1040400,"title":"","content":"Considering that in M20 you can regain 4 WP in a scene (technically the book doesn't even limit these at all, it would just be narratively odd to have multiple chances per scene for something so significant) if you do something that qualifies as a significant personal success that also affirms your nature, as well as 1 WP per decent night's rest, I disagree with the potency argument here. M20's Destiny Background also lets you roll it's rating (at a high difficulty sure) and regain WP if you've run out.<br /> <br /> As well.. mages don't need WP like many other splats do. They don't have powers with a default WP cost. WP is used either as a bonus, or as a way to ignore a complicated.<br /> <br /> So WP might be valuable, but Mage isn't really isn't the game where you see the worst of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T00:55:01-08:00","id":1040486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039219-why-i-hate-sorcerers-rules-or-why-they-don-t-fit-in-mage?p=1040018#post1040018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hum... I see. That indeed seems about right than.<br /> <br /> But if so, why cant Mages learn sorcery paths?<br /> <br /> Or is the Avatar &quot;alergic&quot; to static magic?<br /> <br /> And, if that last option is the case, shouldn't Mage ghouls have a ban on learning disciplines? (and the same restrictions for kinfolk Mages to learn gifts or kinain to learn cantrips - althouth there is a lot of discussion about those traits for Mages, but at least ghouls CAN learn disciplines despite the Awakened status)</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSorcerer Revised do go into it a bit with 'struggling awake' and similar merits and mechanics. In the case of Ghouls, the 'borrowed' and temporary powers can have a very steep price. (IMO, a little too steep and heavy handed in the 'Developers hate crossover' phase.) that also goes away while leaving an addiction behind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}